ivate network, returning host-identifying content\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"httpd installed and configured to listen on 8080 on both nodes, each serving a page with its own hostname/IP ('Hello from node2/node3'). Confirmed reachable from node1 immediately after setup and again after each node's restart (httpd active, serving correct content), and the after-executor listening-sockets snapshot shows httpd bound to *:8080 on both nodes.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-9906cf651ae04e45\",\"cmd-884c119b051d4c98\",\"cmd-d5019f110a8b437d\",\"cmd-077c6d8b53ec4d5b\",\"cmd-3dc252542efe4ad5\",\"global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets\",\"global:after_executor:node3:listening-sockets\"]},{\"id\":\"req-2\",\"requirement\":\"node1 presents a single entry point on TCP 80 of its management address that load-balances across node2 and node3\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"HAProxy (os-haproxy plugin) was configured on node1 with a frontend bound to 10.100.183.10:80 (the LAN/management address) and a round-robin backend pool containing node2 and node3. After resolving a config-validation bug (missing required connectionBehaviour field) and freeing port 80 by disabling the WebGUI HTTP redirect, HAProxy bound to 10.100.183.10:80 and local curl requests alternated between node2 and node3 responses, both immediately after deployment and after node1's own restart.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-d22225da40f649c3\",\"cmd-4aa7cde73b6c4c33\",\"cmd-89805e84c0914924\",\"cmd-5dafa152437b4209\"]},{\"id\":\"req-3\",\"requirement\":\"node4 receives answers from each of node2 and node3 through node1's single entry point\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Repeated curl loops from node4 to http://10.100.183.10:80/ show alternating 'Hello from node2' and 'Hello from node3' responses, both immediately after the HAProxy fix and after every subsequent node restart including node1's own restart, confirming stable end-to-end load-balanced connectivity.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-f3d8a1